321	## Updating & Uninstalling Desktop Commander
322	
323	### Automatic Updates (Options 1, 2, 3, 4 & 6)
324	**Options 1 (npx), Option 2 (bash installer), 3 (Smithery), 4 (manual config), and 6 (Docker)** automatically update to the latest version whenever you restart Claude. No manual intervention needed.
325	
326	### Manual Updates (Option 5)
327	- **Option 5 (local checkout):** `cd DesktopCommanderMCP && git pull && npm run setup`
328	
329	### Uninstalling Desktop Commander
330	#### 🤖 Automatic Uninstallation (Recommended)
331	
332	The easiest way to completely remove Desktop Commander:
333	
334	```bash
335	npx @wonderwhy-er/desktop-commander@latest remove
336	```
337	
338	This automatic uninstaller will:
339	- ✅ Remove Desktop Commander from Claude's MCP server configuration
340	- ✅ Create a backup of your Claude config before making changes
341	- ✅ Provide guidance for complete package removal
342	- ✅ Restore from backup if anything goes wrong
343	
344	#### 🔧 Manual Uninstallation
345	
346	If the automatic uninstaller doesn't work or you prefer manual removal:
347	
348	##### Remove from Claude Configuration
349	
350	1. **Locate your Claude Desktop config file:**
351	  - **macOS:** `~/Library/Application Support/Claude/claude_desktop_config.json`
352	  - **Windows:** `%APPDATA%\Claude\claude_desktop_config.json`
353	  - **Linux:** `~/.config/Claude/claude_desktop_config.json`
354	
355	2. **Edit the config file:**
356	  - Open the file in a text editor
357	  - Find and remove the `"desktop-commander"` entry from the `"mcpServers"` section
358	  - Save the file
359	
360	  **Example - Remove this section:**
361	  ```json
362	  {
363	      "desktop-commander": {
364	        "command": "npx",
365	        "args": ["@wonderwhy-er/desktop-commander@latest"]
366	      }
367	  }
368	  ```
369	
370	Close and restart Claude Desktop to complete the removal.
371	
372	#### 🆘 Troubleshooting
373	
374	**If automatic uninstallation fails:**
375	- Use manual uninstallation as a fallback
376	
377	**If Claude won't start after uninstalling:**
378	- Restore the backup config file created by the uninstaller
379	- Or manually fix the JSON syntax in your claude_desktop_config.json
380	
381	**Need help?**
382	- Join our Discord community: https://discord.com/invite/kQ27sNnZr7
